    passageB1: `<p>Many people today are feeling <strong>stressed</strong>. Studies show that a lot of this stress comes from their jobs. It seems that many people are working too hard, and this is <strong>bad for their health</strong>.</p>

<p>Experts say that there is too much <strong>pressure</strong> on workers. For example, in some jobs, like sales, workers have to reach <strong>unrealistic goals</strong>. People are trying to do things that are too difficult, and this makes them sick.</p>

<p>In many countries, people are working longer <strong>hours</strong>. Some workers need to do this to finish their work. Others think that if they stay late, their boss will be <strong>impressed</strong> and give them a better job. This is called '<strong>presenteeism</strong>' - being at work for a long time.</p>

<p>Working too much can make people very <strong>tired</strong>. Some people cannot sleep well (<strong>insomnia</strong>). When they go home, they cannot <strong>relax</strong>. They keep thinking about work problems.</p>

<p>In the past, people could forget about work when they went on <strong>holiday</strong>. But now, with mobile phones and email, it is difficult to <strong>leave work behind</strong>. It is hard to stop thinking about it.</p>

<p>Our bodies and minds cannot work too hard forever. People reach a point where they cannot <strong>cope</strong>. They need to take time off work. Some people get <strong>burn-out</strong>, and some become <strong>mentally ill</strong>. A study showed that stress can make our bodies <strong>weaker</strong> and more likely to get sick.</p>

<p>The British Health and Safety Executive says that 60% of people who are <strong>absent</strong> from work are away because of stress. We need to <strong>take stress seriously</strong> and think about how we work. Working hard is important, but our health is more important than being <strong>productive</strong>.</p>`,
    translationB1: `<p>Bugungi kunda ko'pchilik odamlar <strong>stress</strong>ni his qilmoqdalar. Tadqiqotlar shuni ko'rsatadiki, bu stressning ko'p qismi ularning ishlaridan kelib chiqadi. Ko'rinishicha, ko'pchilik juda ko'p ishlamoqda va bu ularning <strong>sog'lig'i uchun yomon</strong>.</p>

<p>Mutaxassislarning aytishicha, ishchilarga juda ko'p <strong>bosim</strong> o'tkazilmoqda. Misol uchun, ba'zi ishlarda, masalan, sotuvda, ishchilar <strong>amalga oshirib bo'lmaydigan maqsadlarga</strong> erishishlari kerak. Odamlar juda qiyin bo'lgan ishlarni qilishga harakat qilmoqdalar va bu ularni kasal qiladi.</p>

<p>Ko'pgina mamlakatlarda odamlar uzoqroq <strong>soatlar</strong> ishlashmoqda. Ba'zi ishchilar o'z ishlarini tugatish uchun buni qilishlari kerak. Boshqalar esa agar ular kech qolsalar, boshliqlariga <strong>ta'sir</strong> qilishadi va ular yaxshiroq ish berishadi deb o'ylashadi. Bu '<strong>presenteeism</strong>' deb ataladi - ishda uzoq vaqt bo'lish.</p>

<p>Haddan tashqari ishlash odamlarni juda <strong>charchatishi</strong> mumkin. Ba'zi odamlar yaxshi uxlolmaydilar (<strong>uyqusizlik</strong>). Ular uyga ketganlarida, <strong>dam ololmaydilar</strong>. Ular doimo ish muammolari haqida o'ylashadi.</p>

<p>Ilgari odamlar <strong>ta'tilga</strong> chiqqanlarida ish haqida unutishlari mumkin edi. Ammo endi, mobil telefonlar va elektron pochta orqali, <strong>ishni orqada qoldirish</strong> qiyin. Bu haqda o'ylashni to'xtatish qiyin.</p>

<p>Bizning tanalarimiz va ongimiz abadiy juda ko'p ishlay olmaydi. Odamlar <strong>bardosh bera olmaydigan</strong> nuqtaga etadilar. Ular ishdan dam olishlari kerak. Ba'zi odamlar <strong>charchoq</strong>ni his qilishadi, ba'zilari esa <strong>ruhiy kasal</strong> bo'lib qolishadi. Tadqiqot shuni ko'rsatdiki, stress bizning tanalarimizni <strong>zaiflashtirishi</strong> va kasal bo'lish ehtimolini oshirishi mumkin.</p>

<p>Britaniyaning Sog'liqni saqlash va xavfsizlik bo'yicha ijroiya organi ma'lumotlariga ko'ra, ishdan <strong>yo'q bo'lgan</strong> odamlarning 60 foizi stress tufayli yo'q. Biz <strong>stressga jiddiy qarashimiz</strong> va qanday ishlashimiz haqida o'ylashimiz kerak. Ko'p ishlash muhim, lekin bizning sog'lig'imiz <strong>unumlilikdan</strong> ko'ra muhimroq.</p>`,
