    passageB2: `<p>Increasingly, statistics show that more people are <strong>struggling with stress</strong>, and a significant portion of this is linked to their jobs. It seems that many individuals are working excessively hard, which is negatively <strong>impacting their well-being</strong>.</p>

<p>Experts suggest that employees are under too much pressure these days. In various roles, such as in sales or manufacturing, companies often set <strong>unrealistic targets</strong> for their staff. As a result, people are attempting the impossible, which can lead to illness.</p>

<p>In many countries, a growing number of people are working longer hours. Some employees are compelled to do so to manage their workload, while others believe that staying late will <strong>impress their superiors</strong> and increase their chances of promotion. This practice of spending extra time at work, even when not truly productive, is often referred to as <strong>'presenteeism'</strong>.</p>

<p>Such excessive work often causes extreme tiredness, even <strong>complete exhaustion</strong>, with many individuals also suffering from insomnia. When workers finally get home, instead of relaxing or enjoying their free time, they find it difficult to <strong>switch off</strong> and are still preoccupied with work-related worries.</p>

<p>Many people used to be able to leave the <strong>tensions and anxieties</strong> of the workplace behind when they went on vacation. However, modern communication technologies, such as smartphones and email, have largely made this impossible. We now find it almost impossible to disconnect from our work.</p>

<p>Neither the body nor the mind can sustain excessive workloads indefinitely. Employees eventually reach a point where they can no longer cope and need to take time off. Some may experience <strong>burn-out</strong>, a state of emotional, physical, and mental exhaustion, while others may develop mental health issues. Furthermore, a study conducted by several American universities has indicated that stress can <strong>weaken the immune system</strong>.</p>

<p>The link between work-related stress and illness is supported by findings from the British Health and Safety Executive. Their data suggests that 60 percent of work absences are <strong>attributable to stress</strong>. It is vital that we all take stress seriously and <strong>re-evaluate</strong> the ethics of modern working conditions. While hard work is important, we must recognize that even productivity is less important than our health and <strong>overall quality of life</strong>. Companies need to <strong>prioritize employee wellness</strong> and foster a more supportive work environment to <strong>counteract the detrimental effects</strong> of chronic stress.</p>`,
    translationB2: `<p>Statistikalar tobora ko'proq odamlar <strong>stress bilan kurashayotganini</strong> ko'rsatmoqda va buning katta qismi ularning ishi bilan bog'liq. Ko'rinishicha, ko'pchilik haddan tashqari ko'p ishlamoqda, bu esa ularning <strong>farovonligiga salbiy ta'sir ko'rsatmoqda</strong>.</p>

<p>Mutaxassislarning fikricha, hozirgi kunda xodimlar haddan tashqari bosim ostida. Sotuv yoki ishlab chiqarish kabi turli sohalarda kompaniyalar ko'pincha xodimlar uchun <strong>amalga oshirib bo'lmaydigan maqsadlar</strong> qo'yishadi. Natijada, odamlar imkonsiz narsaga urinishmoqda, bu esa kasallikka olib kelishi mumkin.</p>

<p>Ko'pgina mamlakatlarda tobora ko'proq odamlar uzoqroq ishlashmoqda. Ba'zi xodimlar ish yukini boshqarish uchun shunday qilishga majbur bo'lishsa, boshqalari kechgacha qolish <strong>rahbarlariga taassurot qoldiradi</strong> va lavozimda ko'tarilish imkoniyatini oshiradi deb hisoblashadi. Ishda unumli bo'lmasa ham, qo'shimcha vaqt o'tkazish amaliyoti ko'pincha <strong>"presenteeizm"</strong> deb ataladi.</p>

<p>Bunday haddan tashqari ish ko'pincha juda charchoqqa, hatto <strong>butunlay holdan toyishga</strong> olib keladi, ko'plab odamlar uyqusizlikdan ham aziyat chekishadi. Ishchilar nihoyat uyga kelgach, dam olish yoki bo'sh vaqtlaridan zavqlanish o'rniga, <strong>o'zlarini chalg'itishni</strong> qiyin deb bilishadi va hali ham ish bilan bog'liq tashvishlar bilan band bo'lishadi.</p>

<p>Ko'pchilik odamlar ta'tilga chiqqanlarida ish joyidagi <strong>taranglik va xavotirlarni</strong> ortda qoldira olishardi. Biroq, zamonaviy aloqa texnologiyalari, masalan, smartfonlar va elektron pochta, buni asosan imkonsiz qilib qo'ydi. Hozir biz ishdan uzilishni deyarli imkonsiz deb bilamiz.</p>

<p>Na tana, na aql haddan tashqari ish yukini cheksiz ko'tara olmaydi. Xodimlar oxir-oqibat bardosh bera olmaydigan nuqtaga yetishadi va dam olishga muhtoj bo'lishadi. Ba'zilar <strong>charchoqdan yonib ketishlari</strong> mumkin, bu hissiy, jismoniy va ruhiy charchoq holati, boshqalarda esa ruhiy salomatlik bilan bog'liq muammolar paydo bo'lishi mumkin. Bundan tashqari, bir nechta Amerika universitetlari tomonidan o'tkazilgan tadqiqot shuni ko'rsatdiki, stress <strong>immunitet tizimini zaiflashtirishi</strong> mumkin.</p>

<p>Ish bilan bog'liq stress va kasallik o'rtasidagi bog'liqlik Britaniya Sog'liqni saqlash va xavfsizlik boshqarmasi tomonidan olib borilgan topilmalar bilan tasdiqlangan. Ularning ma'lumotlariga ko'ra, ishda bo'lmaslikning 60 foizi <strong>stress bilan bog'liq</strong>. Barchamiz stressga jiddiy e'tibor qaratishimiz va zamonaviy ish sharoitlarining axloqini <strong>qayta baholashimiz</strong> juda muhim. Qattiq mehnat muhim bo'lsa-da, hatto unumdorlik ham sog'lig'imiz va <strong>hayotimizning umumiy sifatidan</strong> kam ahamiyatga ega ekanligini tan olishimiz kerak. Kompaniyalar <strong>xodimlar salomatligini ustuvor vazifa sifatida belgilashi</strong> va surunkali stressning <strong>zararli oqibatlariga qarshi kurashish</strong> uchun yanada qo'llab-quvvatlovchi ish muhitini yaratishi kerak.</p>`,
