    passageC1: `<p>Mounting evidence suggests that workplace stress is reaching epidemic proportions, with a discernible upswing in the number of individuals <strong>succumbing to</strong> its debilitating effects. A significant portion of this stress, it would seem, <strong>stems directly from</strong> the pressures inherent in contemporary employment. The relentless pursuit of productivity, coupled with increasingly demanding workloads, is demonstrably taking a <strong>considerable toll</strong> on the well-being of the workforce.</p><p>Experts increasingly <strong>attribute</strong> this phenomenon to the <strong>unremitting pressure</strong> placed upon employees across various sectors. In fields such as sales and production, for instance, the imposition of <strong>patently unrealistic targets</strong> is commonplace. Consequently, individuals find themselves <strong>endeavouring to achieve</strong> the impossible, thereby jeopardizing their health in the process. The expectation to consistently <strong>exceed expectations</strong>, while perhaps beneficial to the bottom line, can have devastating consequences for individual employees.</p><p>Furthermore, the trend towards extended working hours is becoming increasingly pervasive across numerous nations. Whether driven by the necessity to manage an overwhelming workload or by the perceived need to impress superiors through <strong>conspicuous presenteeism</strong>, the result is the same: an erosion of work-life balance. This culture of <strong>prolonged exposure</strong> to the workplace can lead to a host of negative outcomes, both for the individual and, ultimately, for the organisation.</p><p>The consequences of such overwork often manifest as profound fatigue and even complete exhaustion, frequently accompanied by debilitating insomnia. Upon returning home, individuals find themselves unable to <strong>disentangle themselves from</strong> work-related anxieties, their minds remaining <strong>preoccupied with</strong> unresolved issues and impending deadlines. The mental and emotional residue of the workday lingers, preventing genuine rest and recuperation.</p><p>The traditional respite afforded by holidays has, unfortunately, been <strong>rendered largely obsolete</strong> by the pervasive influence of modern communication technologies. Mobile phones and email have effectively blurred the boundaries between work and leisure, making it exceedingly difficult to <strong>completely disconnect from</strong> professional obligations. The expectation of constant availability serves only to exacerbate the underlying stress.</p><p>Neither the human body nor the mind is capable of enduring such sustained pressure indefinitely. Eventually, individuals reach a breaking point, necessitating periods of absence from work. Some may experience <strong>full-blown burnout</strong>, while others may develop mental health issues. Moreover, research from American universities has indicated that chronic stress can significantly <strong>compromise the immune system</strong>, rendering individuals more susceptible to illness.</p><p>The correlation between workplace stress and illness is further substantiated by data from the British Health and Safety Executive, which suggests that a substantial proportion of work absences – as much as 60% – are attributable to stress-related conditions. It is therefore imperative that we <strong>address</strong> stress with the seriousness it warrants and critically re-evaluate the prevailing ethos of modern working conditions. While diligence and dedication are undoubtedly valuable assets, it is crucial to recognise that even enhanced productivity must never <strong>supersede</strong> the paramount importance of individual health and well-being.</p>`,
    translationC1: `<p>So‘nggi dalillar shuni ko‘rsatadiki, ish joyidagi stress epidemik darajaga yetmoqda, uning zaiflashtiruvchi ta’siriga <strong>berilayotgan</strong> odamlar soni sezilarli darajada ortib bormoqda. Ko‘rinishidan, bu stressning katta qismi bevosita zamonaviy ish bilan ta’minlashdagi bosimdan <strong>kelib chiqadi</strong>. Ish unumdorligini tinimsiz oshirishga intilish, ortib borayotgan ish hajmi bilan birgalikda ishchi kuchining farovonligiga <strong>sezilarli ta’sir</strong> ko‘rsatmoqda.</p><p>Mutaxassislar tobora ortib borayotgan bu hodisani turli sohalarda ishlaydigan xodimlarga <strong>doimiy bosim</strong> o‘tkazilayotgani bilan <strong>izohlashmoqda</strong>. Masalan, sotuv va ishlab chiqarish kabi sohalarda <strong>oshkora real bo‘lmagan maqsadlar</strong> qo‘yilishi odatiy holga aylangan. Natijada, odamlar imkonsiz narsaga <strong>erishishga harakat qilishadi</strong> va shu bilan birga o‘z sog‘lig‘ini xavf ostiga qo‘yishadi. Doimiy ravishda <strong>kutilganidan yuqori natijalarga erishish</strong>, ehtimol, foydaga foyda keltirishi mumkin, ammo bu alohida xodimlar uchun halokatli oqibatlarga olib kelishi mumkin.</p><p>Bundan tashqari, ko‘plab davlatlarda ish vaqtini uzaytirish tendentsiyasi tobora keng tarqalmoqda. Haddan tashqari ish hajmini boshqarish zarurati yoki <strong>ko‘zga tashlanadigan hozirlik</strong> orqali rahbarlarga taassurot qoldirish zarurati tufayli bo‘ladimi, natija bir xil: ish va hayot muvozanatining buzilishi. Ish joyiga <strong>uzoq vaqt ta’sir qilish</strong> madaniyati ham shaxs, ham tashkilot uchun salbiy oqibatlarga olib kelishi mumkin.</p><p>Bunday haddan tashqari ishlashning oqibatlari ko‘pincha kuchli charchoq va hatto to‘liq holdan toyish, ko‘pincha esa uyqusizlik bilan birga namoyon bo‘ladi. Uyga qaytgach, odamlar o‘zlarini ish bilan bog‘liq tashvishlardan <strong>qutula olmaydilar</strong>, ularning ongida hal qilinmagan muammolar va yaqinlashib kelayotgan muddatlar <strong>band bo‘lib qoladi</strong>. Ish kunining ruhiy va hissiy qoldiqlari uzoq vaqt saqlanib qolib, haqiqiy dam olish va tiklanishga to‘sqinlik qiladi.</p><p>Afsuski, ta’tillar tomonidan taqdim etiladigan an’anaviy dam olish zamonaviy aloqa texnologiyalarining keng ta’siri tufayli <strong>deyarli yo‘qqa chiqarildi</strong>. Mobil telefonlar va elektron pochta ish va dam olish o‘rtasidagi chegaralarni xiralashtirdi va professional majburiyatlardan <strong>butunlay uzilib qolishni</strong> juda qiyinlashtirdi. Doimiy ravishda mavjud bo‘lish umidi shunchaki asosiy stressni kuchaytiradi.</p><p>Na inson tanasi, na aqli bunday doimiy bosimga cheksiz bardosh bera olmaydi. Oxir-oqibat, odamlar sinish nuqtasiga yetib boradilar va bu ishdan uzoqda bo‘lish davrini talab qiladi. Ba’zilar <strong>to‘liq yonib ketishni</strong> boshdan kechirishi mumkin, boshqalarda esa ruhiy salomatlik bilan bog‘liq muammolar paydo bo‘lishi mumkin. Bundan tashqari, Amerika universitetlarining tadqiqotlari shuni ko‘rsatdiki, surunkali stress immunitet tizimiga <strong>jiddiy zarar yetkazishi</strong> va odamlarni kasalliklarga ko‘proq moyil qilishi mumkin.</p><p>Ish joyidagi stress va kasallik o‘rtasidagi bog‘liqlik Buyuk Britaniya Sog‘liqni saqlash va Xavfsizlik Ijroiya organining ma’lumotlari bilan ham tasdiqlanadi, bu ma’lumotlarga ko‘ra, ishdan qolishning katta qismi – 60 foizgacha – stress bilan bog‘liq holatlarga bog‘liq. Shuning uchun biz stressga unga loyiq bo‘lgan jiddiylik bilan <strong>yondashishimiz</strong> va zamonaviy ish sharoitlarining hukmron etosini tanqidiy baholashimiz kerak. Mehnatsevarlik va fidoyilik, shubhasiz, qimmatli fazilatlar bo‘lsa-da, hatto oshirilgan unumdorlik ham hech qachon shaxsning sog‘lig‘i va farovonligining muhim ahamiyatidan <strong>ustun bo‘lmasligi</strong> kerakligini tan olish muhimdir.</p>`,
